    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Easy Glossary plugin helps you create a glossary of terms and definitions, automatically link terms in your content, display optional tooltips, and render an A–Z index. It includes a Settings page to customize behavior.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin folder to <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code>.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; screen in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Go to Glossary <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> Settings to configure options.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='can%20i%20disable%20auto-linking%3F'>\nCan I disable auto-linking?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. Toggle it off in Glossary <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> Settings.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='does%20it%20work%20with%20any%20theme%3F'>\nDoes it work with any theme?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes, it uses standard hooks and minimal CSS.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='how%20can%20i%20show%20glossary%20archive%3F'>\nHow can I show glossary archive?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>To show the glossary archive, you need to use the shortcode [gseasy_glossary].</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial public release.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "A lightweight, flexible glossary plugin that auto-links terms, shows tooltips, and provides an index shortcode.",
    "description": "<p>Easy Glossary plugin helps you create a glossary of terms and definitions, automatically link terms in your content, display optional tooltips, and render an A–Z index. It includes a Settings page to customize behavior.</p>\n",
